+# HUD Kit export plan
+
+Source: `design/figma/hud-kit.json`, page frame **HUD Kit** (`30:1`), file "Block Builder - UI",
+version `2208815566419836712` (last modified 2026-11-02).
+
+This plan covers every visual on that page. For each one it says whether we **build** it from Roblox
+UI objects or **export** it from Figma as an image. For images it gives the export size, the sprite
+sheet it belongs on (if any), and the ImageLabel properties to set.
+
+## Ground rules
+
+### Sizes: author at 1x, export at 2x
+
+All UI is authored in offset pixels for a 1080p screen. `UI/Screen.luau` adds a `UIScale` that grows
+the UI with the screen's short side, from **1x** (1080p and smaller) up to **2x** (4K), and never
+below 1x. So:
+
+- **UI sizes in this doc** (ImageLabel `Size`, `TileSize`, `SliceScale` maths) are the Figma sizes,
+  1:1. Don't scale them yourself; the UIScale does that.
+- **Image files are exported at 2x the Figma size** so they stay sharp at the 2x maximum. At 1080p
+  the engine draws them at half size, which looks fine.
+- Exceptions are called out: the logo (Roblox's 1024 px upload limit) and the glow (blurry already,
+  so 1x is enough).
+
+### Roblox image limits
+
+- Roblox shrinks any uploaded image larger than **1024 px on either side**. Every file in this plan
+  is 1024 × 1024 or smaller.
+- Export **PNG with a transparent background**. Before exporting a frame, remove its fill unless this
+  doc says the fill is part of the image.
+- **Hide every `Note` text layer before exporting.** Several notes are children of the frame being
+  exported, and some sit outside the frame's bounds, so leaving them visible adds text and can also
+  make the exported image bigger.
+
+### Sprite sheet rules
+
+- A sheet holds images that **appear on screen together**. Images that are only needed in one input
+  mode go on that mode's own sheet, so a player only downloads what their device needs.
+- Every cell has a **2 px transparent margin on each side** (4 px between neighbours). Without it,
+  smoothing pulls in pixels from the neighbouring cell when the engine scales the image down.
+- Build each sheet in Figma as a **1x frame**: cells are the icon's 1x size plus 1 px on each side.
+  Then export the frame at **2x**. The pixel positions below are for the exported 2x PNG. They are
+  the values for `ImageRectOffset` and `ImageRectSize`.
+- Formula: stride = cell + 4. Cell `(col, row)` sits at `ImageRectOffset = (2 + col × stride, 2 + row × stride)`.
+
+### ImageLabel defaults (apply to every image below unless stated)
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `BackgroundTransparency` | `1` |
+| `ScaleType` | `Stretch` |
+| `ResampleMode` | `Default` |
+| `ImageColor3` | `255, 255, 255` |
+| `ImageTransparency` | `0` |
+
+### Font
+
+Builder Sans is built into Roblox:
+`Font.new("rbxasset://fonts/families/BuilderSans.json", <weight>)`.
+
