+## 2. Prompts / Keyboard: build
+
+Each key is a rounded rectangle with a stroke and a text label. Roblox UI objects can draw all of
+that. Building them keeps the text sharp at any scale and avoids 10 images.
+
+Keys: `B`, `I`, `E`, `Q`, `1`, `2`, `3` (40 × 40) and `Esc`, `Tab`, `Shift` (56 × 40).
+
+| Object | Properties |
+|---|---|
+| `Frame` | `Size` 40 × 40 (or 56 × 40), `BackgroundColor3` 235, 237, 242, `BorderSizePixel` 0 |
+| └ `UICorner` | `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 6)` |
+| └ `UIStroke` | `Thickness` 2, `Color` 153, 157, 171, `ApplyStrokeMode` Border, `BorderStrokePosition` Inner (Figma's stroke is inside the 40 px) |
+| └ `TextLabel` | `Size` fromScale(1, 1), `BackgroundTransparency` 1, `Text` = key name, Builder Sans **Bold**, `TextSize` 18, `TextColor3` 31, 33, 41, centred both ways |
+
+If `BorderStrokePosition` isn't available in your Studio build, make the Frame 4 px smaller
+(36 × 36 / 52 × 36) so the outside stroke brings it back to the designed size. At 4K, check in the
+device emulator that the stroke thickness scales with the UIScale.
