+## 6. Panel / Ornate: export as a 9-slice, `panel_ornate.png`
+
+**Why export:** the gold corner flourishes are custom vectors. **Why 9-slice:** the note says the
+panel stretches from 240 × 160 up to 960 × 640 and the corners must not stretch. With 9-slice the
+corners stay fixed while the edges and centre (solid fill plus straight stroke) stretch cleanly.
+
+**Figma:** duplicate the `Panel / Ornate` frame (40:137) and resize the copy to **112 × 112**
+(48 px corner + 16 px middle + 48 px corner). Move the corners so each sits flush in its corner:
+Corner 1 at (0, 0), Corner 2 at (64, 0), Corner 3 at (0, 64), Corner 4 at (64, 64). Keep the frame's
+fill (33, 27, 20) and its 4 px inside stroke (217, 172, 81), because both are part of the image.
+Hide the Note. Export at **2x → 224 × 224 px**.
+
+Standalone file, not on a sheet. It's only used for dialogs, and keeping it alone keeps the slice
+setup simple.
+
+**ImageLabel:**
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `Size` | the dialog size, anywhere from 240 × 160 to 960 × 640 |
+| `ScaleType` | `Slice` |
+| `SliceCenter` | `Rect.new(96, 96, 128, 128)` (image pixels: the 48 px corners × 2) |
+| `SliceScale` | `0.5` (the image is 2x, so corners draw at 48 UI px, and at 96 screen px when the UIScale is 2x) |
+
