+## 7. Slot / Empty: export, `slot_empty.png`
+
+**Why export:** the border is **dashed** (8 on, 6 off). `UIStroke` can't draw dashes.
+
+**Size:** the note says the slot size is a player setting from 80 to 128. The largest it can appear
+on screen is 128 × the 2x UIScale = 256 px, so export it at that size. The slot is always square,
+so it scales evenly. The dashes and the 2 px line get a little thinner at 80 and thicker at 128;
+see Open questions.
+
+**Figma:** select `Slot / Empty` (40:139), hide its Note (it sits outside the frame and would be
+included), and set the stroke opacity from 30% to **100%** (the transparency is applied in Roblox
+instead, which avoids baking a faint, banded alpha). Export with a fixed width of **256w → 256 × 256 px**.
+
+**ImageLabel:**
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `Size` | `UDim2.fromOffset(slotSize, slotSize)`, where `slotSize` is 80–128 |
+| `ImageTransparency` | `0.7` (matches Figma's 30% white) |
+
