+## 9. Background / Dot Grid: export one tile, `tile_dot_grid.png`
+
+**Why export:** Roblox can't draw a dot pattern. **Why a tile:** the note says it repeats behind every
+full-screen menu at any screen size, so we export one repeating cell and let `ScaleType = Tile` fill
+the screen. Tiled images can't come from a sprite sheet, so this is its own file.
+
+The sample is 2 px dots every 24 px; each dot sits 11 px into its 24 px cell.
+
+**Figma:** make a new **24 × 24** frame with no fill and a 2 × 2 white ellipse at (11, 11), at
+**100% opacity** (the sample's 5% frame opacity is applied in Roblox instead). Export at
+**2x → 48 × 48 px** (the dot covers pixels 22–25).
+
+**ImageLabel:**
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `Size` | `UDim2.fromScale(1, 1)` (covers the menu) |
+| `ScaleType` | `Tile` |
+| `TileSize` | `UDim2.fromOffset(24, 24)` |
+| `ImageTransparency` | `0.95` (Figma's 5% opacity) |
