+## 12. Item Portraits: export one file per item, `item_<name>.png`
+
+**Why export:** these are raster art (image fills).
+
+**Why not a sheet:** the note says there are 120 portraits, more are added every update, and the
+detail pane shows **one at a time**. With 256 px cells a 1024 px sheet holds only 16, so showing one
+item would download a sheet of 16 unused ones, and every update would mean repacking the sheets
+and changing offsets. One file per item is simpler and loads less.
+
+**Figma:** export each `Item Portrait/<Name>` rectangle at **2x → 256 × 256 px**, with its 12 px
+rounded corners baked in (24 px in the file). Name the files in lowercase:
+`item_torch.png`, `item_ladder.png`, `item_door.png`, `item_fence.png`, `item_chest.png`,
+`item_bed.png`, and so on for all 120. Check that the source art behind each image fill is at least
+256 × 256, or the export will be upscaled and blurry.
+
+Upload them in bulk with the Asset Manager's Bulk Import.
+
+**ImageLabel:**
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `Size` | `UDim2.fromOffset(128, 128)` |
+| `Image` | set at runtime from the item → asset ID table |
+
